{{Quote|We're checking to see if QFD or their erstwhile partners, Pammant Docks, might have supervised the reassembly.|An Imperial technician informs [[Wilhuff Tarkin|Tarkin]] of the investigation into Pammant Docks|<ref name="Trkn" />}}
'''Pammant Docks''', also known as the '''Pammant Shipyards''', was a shipwright company that at one time held a partnership with the [[Quarren]] organization known as the [[Free Dac Volunteers Engineering Corps]]. During the [[Clone Wars]], Pammant Docks was allied with the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]],<ref name="Trkn" /> being represented by the [[Quarren]] official [[Tikkes]].<ref name="OF84">{{GermanFanCite|84|Database}}</ref>

While the early [[Confederacy of Independent Systems Navy|Confederacy navy]] was made up of heavily armed [[bulk transport]]s from CIS member corporations, Pammant Docks and other allies constructed [[capital ship]]s to create a creditable [[navy]] for the Separatists,<ref name="Trkn" /> such as the [[Subjugator-class heavy cruiser|''Subjugator''-class heavy cruiser]].<ref name="Collapse" /> These new [[starship]]s were crewed by [[B1-series battle droid]]s and filled with a variety of [[starfighter]]s. The Separatist allied Quarren at Pammant Docks allowed for a large number of starships to be produced quickly for the Separatists.<ref name="Rise" /> After a [[Berch Teller's warship|warship]] assembled from old Confederacy of Independent Systems' vessels [[Attack on Sentinel Base|attacked]] the Imperial facility [[Sentinel Base]], the [[Galactic Empire]] began looking into if Pammant Docks or the volunteers had been involved in the [[warship]]'s assembly.<ref name="Trkn" />

==Behind the scenes==
Pammant Docks was first mentioned in the new ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[canon]] in [[Tarkin (novel)|''Tarkin'']], a [[2014]] novel written by [[James Luceno]] and published by [[Del Rey]].<ref name="Trkn" /> It was originally mentioned in [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] continuity in ''[[Star Wars: Revenge of the Sith Incredible Cross-Sections]]'', a [[2005]] reference book written by [[Curtis Saxton]] and published by [[Dorling Kindersley]] as part of the ''[[Incredible Cross-Sections]]'' series.<ref name="ROTS:ICS">''[[Star Wars: Revenge of the Sith Incredible Cross-Sections]]''</ref>

